  "body": "The \"Event structure\" subsection \"Size limits\" in the C-S API spec states some data size limits for events and for some of the events' fields. There should be an explanation of what a homeserver is expected to do if it receives an event which violates one of these limits, as well as how clients and servers should behave when wanting to send an event that would violate the limits, e.g. an event with an extremely long message body.\n\n(Imported from https://matrix.org/jira/browse/SPEC-406)\n\n(Reported by Jimmy Cuadra)\n",
